  "id": "after-nystagmus",
  "term": "after-nystagmus",
  "definition": "After-nystagmus, specifically optokinetic after-nystagmus, is the continued rhythmic eye movement that gradually fades after a moving visual stimulus is suddenly stopped. It reflects a slow discharge of the neural system involved in integrating motion signals, and its time constant is described as shorter in people with vestibular disorders than in healthy controls.",
